<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis world's top cargo airport in Jan-Feb - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis world's top cargo airport in Jan-Feb - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-February 1997, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI) in a survey of 486 airports worldwide.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in  January-February 1997, with the volume they handled, their ranking and the percentage change on January-February 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1 (1)  Memphis	    337,514 tonnes  up  20.1 pct</p>
<p>    2 (3)  Los Angeles	273,538 tonnes  up   8.7</p>
<p>    3 (2)  Miami		265,004 tonnes  down 0.4</p>
<p>    4 (4)  Tokyo-Narita     249,948 tonnes  up   5.4</p>
<p>    5 (5)  New York JFK     239,973 tonnes  up   2.0</p>
<p>    6 (8)  Hong Kong	  234,117 tonnes  up  13.7</p>
<p>    7 (7)  Frankfurt	  225,713 tonnes  up   0.7</p>
<p>    8 (9)  Seoul		223,256 tonnes  up  20.3</p>
<p>    9 (6)  Louisville	 218,743 tonnes  down 2.5</p>
<p>   10 (12) Singapore	  195,974 tonnes  up  11.8</p>
<p>   11 (10) Chicago	    194,217 tonnes  up   7.1</p>
<p>   12 (11) Amsterdam	  180,338 tonnes  up   2.3</p>
<p>   13 (13) London Heathrow  179,198 tonnes  up   4.3</p>
<p>   14 (16) Anchorage*	 168,958 tonnes  up  23.3</p>
<p>   15 (15) New York Newark  155,844 tonnes  up   6.8</p>
<p>   16 (14) Paris CDG	  153,804 tonnes  up   4.4</p>
<p>   17 (17) Atlanta	    128,262 tonnes  up   3.0</p>
<p>   18 (18) Dayton	     126,191 tonnes  up   8.8</p>
<p>   19 (19) Dallas Ft Worth  120,968 tonnes  up   9.2</p>
<p>   20 (20) Taipei		20,346 tonnes  up  15.3</p>
<p>* includes freight and mail in transit as well as loaded and unloaded cargo</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
